CORE
main.c
--pointer-check
^\[main\.assertion\.1\] line \d+ assertion g->vptr->call\(\) == 2: SUCCESS$
^\[main\.assertion\.2\] line \d+ assertion g->vptr->call\(\) == 3: FAILURE$
^\*\* 1 of \d+ failed
^VERIFICATION FAILED$
^EXIT=10$
^SIGNAL=0$
--
dereference failure: .*: FAILURE$
--
With field sensitivity the members of a union and the elements of a small
array are separate symbols whose value sets are recorded under their own
names (`fn..st..ptrs[[0]]').  A pointer read through the union as another
type looked the member up as `fn.st.ptrs[]', found nothing and assumed an
unknown target, so the call through the read vtable pointer failed its
dereference checks.
